From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:54:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): watch a session's pull requests until they're
 green

After an agent opens a PR, someone still has to babysit it: notice a red
check, a review or a merge conflict, and nudge the session to deal with it.
Upstream refreshes a session's stored PRs after each turn, shows them in the
Pull Requests panel, and has trigger automations and timers, but nothing
tells a session about its own PRs. This adds an opt-in watch that does, for
any harness, behind the default-off `pr_watch` feature.

- A "Watch PRs" chip in the composer bar, next to the PR link, opens a
  popover with "All PRs in this session" (every PR it links now and any it
  opens later) and one box per open PR with its title, CI state and
  wake-ups used. Unchecking one PR while "All" is on keeps the rest. The
  chip reads "Watching N PRs" while active; the PR panel keeps a "Watch
  until green" switch bound to the same state.
- A per-server poller (`omnigent/server/pr_watch.py`) takes the session's
  PRs from the server's stored list, which the runner's reports and the
  turn-end refresh keep current, and asks the listed-session refresher for
  a read while "All" is on or the list is not imported yet. An unlink in
  the Pull Requests tab ends a watch, and a PR stored as merged or closed
  is skipped without asking the host. Each watched PR is read through the
  panel's path (runner, else host, with the host's account), sharing a
  read with an open panel, so it adds no credentials.
- It reports failed checks on the head commit, comments and reviews from
  the repository's owners, members and collaborators, and merge conflicts
  once each, coalesced across PRs into one `[System: PR watch ...]`
  message. The message goes through the normal message path as the
  session's owner, so input policies apply, and only while the session is
  idle: not during a turn, and not while it waits on an approval or a
  question (the signals a trigger automation waits on). Anyone else's
  comment text never reaches the agent.
- Each PR's watch ends with a transcript note that starts no turn when its
  checks pass with no changes requested, it is merged or closed, its
  wake-up budget (default 10) is spent, checks cannot be read, or five
  wake-ups in a row could not be delivered. The ended state is kept so
  "All" does not pick the PR up again.
- State lives in server-reserved session labels, so it survives a restart
  without a migration: `omnigent.pr_watch.mode` for "All", and a URL and a
  state label per PR keyed by a hash of its URL. Forks drop the family, and
  clients cannot write it except through GET/PUT/PATCH/DELETE
  /v1/sessions/{id}/pr-watch. Reading needs read access; changing a watch
  is for the session's owner only, like the other pull request changes on
  a shared session, since wake-ups are sent as the owner.
- The GitHub payload gains `mergeable`, each reviewer's `submitted_at`,
  and comment and review `author_association`, so conflicts, repeat
  reviews and trusted authors are detectable.

Interval and budget: OMNIGENT_PR_WATCH_INTERVAL_S (90) and
OMNIGENT_PR_WATCH_MAX_WAKES (10).

Not upstream yet: not proposed upstream yet.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
